; Mutating (in-place) Ops: the kernel reads and overwrites ONE storage —
; its first operand's — so they are matched only when the output layout
; EQUALS the mutated operand's layout (and the write is injective). No
; output Layout field: the input LayoutTensor determines it, so consing
; stays truthful. Binary forms mutate operand 1 and read operand 2 from
; anywhere.
(constructor LayoutTensorOpSqrtMutatingGeneric (LayoutTensor) LayoutTensorOp)
